Maze Linux installer customization
==================================

The installer is launched with the command:

    maze-install

It is a thin wrapper around `archinstall`. Run on its own it opens the
interactive archinstall TUI. To customize the install, drop either of these
files into this directory (/etc/maze-installer):

    maze.json    -> forwarded to `archinstall --config FILE`
    creds.json   -> forwarded to `archinstall --creds FILE`

Both are optional. If present, `maze-install` passes them to archinstall;
if absent, the installer is fully interactive.

Templates to copy and edit are provided next to this file:

    maze.json.example
    creds.json.example

Notes
-----
* The archinstall config schema changes between archinstall versions. After
  copying an example, validate it against the archinstall that ships in this
  image:

      archinstall --config /etc/maze-installer/maze.json --dry-run

* A *complete* config + creds lets you run an unattended install:

      maze-install --silent

  A *partial* config simply pre-fills the menu, leaving the rest interactive.

* This data-file layout is intentional: a future Maze Linux GUI front-end can
  generate maze.json / creds.json here, then invoke `maze-install`.
